      "Part 1: Structural Foundations of BEJSON Formats",
      "This chapter defines the core structural specifications of the BEJSON 105 series, contrasting single-entity tables (`105`), primitive metadata configurations (`105a`), and multi-record lightweight database bundles (`105db`). It details universal header contracts, positional matrix layouts where values are decoupled from schema declarations, and exact entity type isolation rules without burying the runtime in validation boilerplate. The discussion then transitions directly into how these standalone documents are orchestrated across complex multi-file file systems.\n\nTarget length: about 150 words.",
