      "3dffa597-4c21-48ff-8de2-e5271d1223a6",
      2,
      "Part 2: Multi-File Database (MFDB) Orchestration and Federation",
      "This chapter examines the Multi-File Database (MFDB) orchestration layer, explaining how a central `104a.mfdb.bejson` manifest coordinates discrete Format `105` entity files into a unified serverless relational graph. It details bidirectional path verification, `_fk` foreign key conventions, and the `Network_Role` Master-Slave topology that maximizes AI context window efficiency through operational structural blindness. This sets the stage for exploring how $O(1)$ memory access speeds are maintained across these federated disk layouts.\n\nTarget length: about 150 words.",
