      "1e5ca4fd-10a2-4f05-a0a2-03b1e8424403",
      3,
      "Part 3: O(1) Field Map Caching and Cryptographic UUID Addressing",
      "This chapter breaks down constant-time $O(1)$ field map caching, an in-memory look-up mechanism that eliminates key-parsing overhead and positional fragility. It explains why traditional index-based access fails under schema evolution and demonstrates how `field_uuid` column fingerprints and `record_uuid` offset resolution guarantee zero-drift addressability across mutations. Understanding these deterministic memory lookups transitions directly into enforcing strict system-wide validation invariants.\n\nTarget length: about 150 words.",
